  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** AI server demand remains robust, as demonstrated by sharp order gains at direct competitors, but Supermicro has not participated equally. Instead, its own standing has been undermined by a prolonged accounting scandal and a looming share-count expansion that threatens heavy dilution. While the broader AI infrastructure theme continues to provide tailwinds, company-specific credibility gaps have caused severe relative underperformance, suggesting the market no longer views Supermicro as a reliable conduit for that demand.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has pursued a massive equity raise and is shadowed by a chip-smuggling probe and unresolved accounting turmoil, deepening a trust deficit with investors. Sustained insider selling and persistent governance overhangs reinforce a narrative of a management team geared toward near-term liquidity rather than rebuilding long-term confidence. Collectively, these actions signal a credibility crisis that has left the company as the riskiest name among AI server peers.",
