        "url": "https://ts2.tech/en/super-micro-stocks-4-gain-hides-a-one-day-rally-and-a-potential-38-share-count-expansion/",
        "snippet": "Super Micro Stock’s 4% Gain Hides a One-Day Rally—and a Potential 38% Share-Count Expansion\n\nDark\n\nLight\n\nToday: 16 July 2026\n\nTechStock²\n\nReal-Time Market Intelligence\n\nTechStock²\n\n13 July 2026\n\nNASDAQ:SMCI· Stock Market\n\n2 mins read\n\n# Super Micro Stock’s 4% Gain Hides a One-Day Rally—and a Potential 38% Share-Count Expansion\n\nhttps://ts2.tech/en/author/jerzy/ by Jerzy Lewandowski\n\nNew York, July 12, 2026, 18:08 EDT\n\nSuper Micro Computer Inc. NASDAQ:SMCI finished Friday at $28.31, up 4.0% for the week. But Wednesday’s 7.3% jump supplied more than the entire gain: excluding that session, the shares lost a compounded 3.1% over the other four trading days. U.S. cash markets were closed Sunday and are scheduled to reopen Monday at 9:30 a.m. EDT.\n\nThat split matters because the wider AI-hardware trade moved faster. Server rival Dell Technologies Inc. NYSE:DELL gained 10.3% for the week, Nvidia Corp. NASDAQ:NVDA rose 8.3%, and the Nasdaq Composite added 1.7%. Supermicro beat the index, but",
        "published_date": "2026-07-12T22:27:14.000Z"
      },
      {
        "title": "SMX First-Half 2026 Results: $50.5M Raised | SMX Stock News",
        "url": "https://www.stocktitan.net/news/SMX/smx-strengthens-balance-sheet-and-advances-global-commercialization-pjmbk7tjf49q.html",
        "snippet": "SMX First-Half 2026 Results: $50.5M Raised | SMX Stock News\n\n# SMX Strengthens Balance Sheet and Advances Global Commercialization Strategy in First Half 2026\n\n(High)\n\n(Very Positive)\n\nTags\n\n## Rhea-AI Summary\n\n- English\n- Arabic\n- French\n- German\n- Italian\n- Korean\n- Spanish\n\nSMX (NASDAQ: SMX) reported first half 2026 results showing a markedly stronger balance sheet and ongoing global expansion. The company raised US$50.5 million under its existing SEPA program, increasing cash and cash equivalents to US$34.5 million. Payables and loans were reduced by 61% to US$8.7 million, while shareholders' equity rose 181% to US$54.4 million. SMX continued expanding across Singapore, the UAE and Japan and invested in Circular Economy, Plastic Credit Token, cyber hardware authentication and digital asset initiatives. According to SMX, the strengthened balance sheet enhances financial flexibility to support commercialization, strategic partnerships and further technology development through 2026.\n",
        "published_date": "2026-07-17T21:00:00.000Z"
